        {
          "id": "setting",
          "type": "story",
          "lines": [
            "Roads can be built to expect human error: a moment of distraction, a tired driver, a misjudged gap.",
            "Let's look at five road features and what they do."
          ],
          "art": {
            "kind": "road-treatment",
            "params": {
              "treatment": "rumble",
              "on": true
            },
            "alt": "Top-down view of a road with rumble strips along the centre line."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "rumble",
          "type": "toggle-lab",
          "prompt": "Rumble strips along the centre line. A tired driver drifts across.",
          "art": {
            "kind": "road-treatment",
            "params": {
              "treatment": "rumble",
              "on": false
            },
            "alt": "Top-down road with centre-line rumble strips shown or hidden."
          },
          "states": [
            {
              "id": "off",
              "label": "Without",
              "params": {
                "on": false
              },
              "caption": "Without them, a drifting car crosses into oncoming traffic silently."
            },
            {
              "id": "on",
              "label": "With",
              "params": {
                "on": true
              },
              "caption": "The noise and shaking wake the driver before they cross. Centre-line strips cut head-on crashes by about {claim:int.fhwa.rumble-centre}."
            }
          ],
          "requireAll": true
        },
        {
